WEBVTT

00:31:55.114 --> 00:32:01.726
(Siren blares,
indistinct radio communications)

00:32:01.750 --> 00:32:03.813
Chris Macklin: Anytime you're taking care

00:32:03.837 --> 00:32:07.069
of men and women
who call 911, or children,

00:32:07.093 --> 00:32:08.274
they're at their worst.

00:32:08.298 --> 00:32:11.056
And you're always supposed
to be at your best.

00:32:11.080 --> 00:32:15.266
AG: Chris Macklin was a paramedic
in Denver, Colorado for 10 years.

00:32:15.290 --> 00:32:18.336
The demands of that job
took a toll on him.

00:32:18.360 --> 00:32:20.543
CM: I didn't know
how to take care of myself,

00:32:20.567 --> 00:32:21.884
because I was so burned out

00:32:21.908 --> 00:32:24.386
and never wanted to work
in that role again.

00:32:24.410 --> 00:32:27.826
AG: He decided to leave that job
and become a firefighter.

00:32:27.850 --> 00:32:30.306
But soon enough,
Chris found that firefighting